# Pre-/post-request scripting, in Lua: a login -> token -> authenticated
# request chain, the pattern for real APIs that issue a session/JWT token on
# login and expect it back as a Bearer token.
#
# Run `make httpbin-up` first. Each request resolves its {{var}} placeholders
# right before it's sent, using whatever client.global currently holds -- so
# this works either way: :HttpSendAll sends both at once, or :HttpSend on
# Login once and then on AuthenticatedRequest as often as you like.
#
# Either way, AuthenticatedRequest's {{auth_token}} is whatever Login's
# post-request script most recently set (persisted in .httpfly/state.json;
# :HttpSessionClear resets it). See docs/scripting.md. See 4_download.http for saving a binary response
# to a file, 6_shell_auth.http for shelling out to an external command in
# a pre-request script instead of an HTTP call, and 7_save_response.http
# for saving a response body yourself from a post-request script.

###
# @name Login
GET http://localhost:8080/uuid HTTP/1.1

> {%
  local json = require("json")
  local data = json.decode(response.body)
  client.global:set("auth_token", data.uuid)
%}

###
# @name AuthenticatedRequest
GET http://localhost:8080/bearer HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
